          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: föhnen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "föhnen — \"to blow-dry\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nach dem Waschen föhnt sie sich die Haare. After washing her hair she blow-dries it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Der Föhn — the hair dryer, and also a warm wind from the mountains."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "föhnen is built on Föhn, a warm dry wind in the mountains, which goes back through Old High German phōnno to Latin favōnius 'mild west wind' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). The hair dryer was named after the wind."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
